  "findings": [
    "The first live production preflight exposed that pressure advance belongs to PrinterExtruder.extruder_stepper on this runtime; direct attributes on PrinterExtruder are unsupported.",
    "Stationary direct-trapq extrusion generated filament motion while recorded X, Y, and Z remained unchanged.",
    "The load-cell response changed during low/high/low extrusion, so the signal is measurable at the tested flows.",
    "Several 500 Hz captures lost responses or had command intervals above 5 ms while trapq work was active; 500 Hz is not yet a validated under-load default.",
    "The single 250 Hz under-load capture returned every requested response, but one cycle is insufficient to validate a production rate.",
    "Near-zero and large isolated excursions persisted during heated and extrusion captures.",
    "Repeated K responses were not repeatable enough to classify a candidate; no PA value was reported.",
    "A follow-up 250 Hz pulse returned 351 responses for 351 requests, but two callbacks shared the same sent time and payload.",
    "The stock CS1237 configuration read 190 instead of 60 after the follow-up pulse, so the planned two-acceleration sweep was aborted after one pulse.",
    "Receive timing and these exploratory outlier windows do not establish ADC conversion freshness or a hardware-safe invalid-read classifier."
  ],
  "analysis_note": "exploratory_outlier_count and exploratory_window_medians use a non-production neighbor heuristic only to summarize signal shape; they are not accepted quality gates."
